( 64-bit numbers as double cells: two stack entries, the low cell below the
  high cell, as in standard Forth. A number ending in a dot is a double
  literal: 1700000000000. -5. 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF. - a dot with digits after
  it, like 1.5, is a float.
  Signed and unsigned: d+ d- ud* d= d0= 2@ 2! 2constant 2variable d>s
  Signed: d< d> d<= d>= dmin dmax d0< m* d/ dmod dnegate dabs s>d d.
  Unsigned: du< du> du<= du>= dumin dumax um* ud/ udmod u>d ud.
  Primitives: d+ d- d< du< m* um* ud* d/ dmod ud/ udmod. )

: s>d dup <0 ;
: u>d 0 ;
: d>s drop ;
: d= rot = >r = r> & ;
: d0= | =0 ;
: d0< swap drop <0 ;
: dnegate 0 0 2swap d- ;
: dabs dup <0 if dnegate fi ;

: d> 2swap d< ;
: d<= d> not ;
: d>= d< not ;
: dmin 2over 2over d> if 2swap fi 2drop ;
: dmax 2over 2over d< if 2swap fi 2drop ;
: d. s" %ld " fmt ;

: du> 2swap du< ;
: du<= du> not ;
: du>= du< not ;
: dumin 2over 2over du> if 2swap fi 2drop ;
: dumax 2over 2over du< if 2swap fi 2drop ;
: ud. s" %lu " fmt ;

( Double-cell memory, using fixed cell-size access. As in standard Forth, 2!
  stores the high cell at addr and the low cell at the next cell. 2variable
  is zero-initialized and stays writable in a ROM image. )
: 2! swap over !c cell + !c ;
: 2@ dup cell + @c swap @c ;
: 2constant >r >r : r> postpone literal r> postpone literal postpone ; ;
: 2variable data-here 2 cells data-allot 0 0 2 pick 2! constant ;
